A||N||4||Daleford||Need directions in Boston, anyone live there?||||5||
Z||000000||Daleford||12-30-2001||03:04 PM||||--- I wish to go to Boston and stay at a particular YMCA. I am re-tracing my youth when 30 years ago I stayed for a couple days in your fair city.  Trouble is I cannot find a YMCA location where I think I stayed.<BR>I know it was within walking distance of the John Hancock tower, and kind of west of it on a wide street. Commonwealth?   Anybody remember a YMCA there?  Thanking you in advance......<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Patrick's Dad||12-30-2001||04:11 PM||||There is a YMCA at 300 Tremont Street, a little less than a mile down the street from the Hancock Tower. Here's a map:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.mapquest.com/maps/map.adp?country=US&address=300+Tremont+Street&city=Boston&state=MA&zipcode=02116&level=3" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mapquest.com/maps/map.adp?country=US&address=300+Tremont+Street&city=Boston&state=MA&zipcode=02116&level=3</A> <P>I remember a YMCA along Comm. Ave, but that may be because you placed a suggestion in my head. I'll have to ask my wife (A Boston native. I'm from the 'burbs.).||||reg||2
Z||000002||LarryB||12-30-2001||06:31 PM||||You're probably thinking of the one on Huntington Ave. not far from the Christian Science plaza and near Northeastern - an area where you want to be alert and keep your wits about you at night.<P>There's also another one near NEMC but that's in Chinatown, to the east of the Hancock Tower.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Daleford||12-30-2001||09:49 PM||||Thanks guys.  Larry, you may have hit it. The Huntington Ave location almost fits.  Only problem...... I seem to recall leaving the Hancock tower, going north, then west to get back to my room. On the map it seems the Y was out around Commonwealth and 2a???<BR>Patrick's Dad, does your wife recall...?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000004||LarryB||12-31-2001||01:06 AM||||That's in the same general area, the Christian Science plaza is on Mass Ave (2A) 6-7 blocks south of Comm Ave, which itself is a couple of blocks south of Beacon St.   If you walked south on Mass Ave from Comm Ave to the intersection with Huntington Ave., you'd look to your right and across Huntington to see that Y, if you turned left and looked up Huntington you'd see the Prudential Tower a ways up.  It's not far either from where the E branch of the Green Line comes above ground.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by LarryB (edited 12-31-2001).]||||reg||1
